# HR-F-06 paper is locked

The Leave Request print layout must stay identical to `EW - HR-F-06 Leave request.docx` on every PC.

Do **not** change shape, size, spacing, padding, row heights, borders, or print layout unless the user explicitly asks.

Locked measurements (from the Word file):

- A4 `210mm × 297mm`, `@page { margin: 0 }`
- Logo from Word header (`assets/hr-f06-logo.png`) at `7mm` from top, `51.22mm × 25.30mm`
- Body top `33.27mm` (title starts here), right `16.26mm`, bottom `25.4mm`, left `17.52mm`
- Title 14pt Calibri `#0D0D0D`; first table top `45.81mm` (title then `7.6mm` gap)
- Table width `174.63mm` (Word 9900 twips); entitlement `174.54mm` — never `width: 100%` on print
- Absence columns `34.55% / 30.91% / 34.55%`
- Cell borders `0.5pt`: **dotted inside**, **solid outside** (Word TableGrid + cell overrides)
- Title 14pt, section headings 12pt bold, body 10pt Calibri
- Data rows `18pt`; section headings emp `22.3pt`, absence `24.05pt`, approvals `22.7pt`, entitle `21.85pt`, HR `24.9pt`
- Emp sig `28.95pt`, approvals `32.1pt`, HR comment `68.1pt`, HR foot `24.45pt`
- Footer `HR-F-06` / `Rev.2` at `6mm` from the bottom edge
- **No yellow fill**, no Word watermark, no sample dates — start/end/HR date cells stay blank until filled
- Print iframe / bake-values path; same CSS for one paper and many papers

Filing completed papers into leave-type sections is list-only. Do not change the paper for that feature.
